  )
end

Tour.Live.panel(fn -> Tour.UI.stack(Enum.map(readme_queries, answer_line)) end)
````

## 4. Many copies

Prometheus discovers the app containers through the Docker socket and labels each series with `pod` (container name), `instance` (IP and port), and `env`.

Counters reset to 0 when a container restarts. `rate()` handles a reset within one series, so take `rate()` per series and then `sum()`; summing first hides the reset. Each container also adds its own set of series. Compose keeps container names across restarts, so new series only appear when scaling up.

**Kill one app container** restarts a container: its raw counter drops to 0, `sum(rate())` stays steady, and `rate(sum())` spikes. **Scale** to 4 raises the raw series count while the rolled-up count stays the same.

```elixir
kill = Kino.Control.button("Kill one app container")

scale_to =
  Kino.Control.form(
    [
      n:
        Kino.Input.select("App containers", Enum.map(1..5, &{&1, Integer.to_string(&1)}),
          default: 4
        )
    ],
    submit: "Scale"
  )

happened = Tour.UI.frame()

crashed = fn
  name, :ok ->
    Tour.UI.note(
      :ok,
      "Crashed `#{name}` with exit code 1. Docker restarts it under the same name, so `pod` keeps its value and the counter starts again from 0."
    )

  _name, {:error, reason} ->
    Tour.UI.note(:error, reason)
end

Kino.listen(kill, fn _click ->
  Tour.UI.draw(happened, fn ->
    case Tour.Docker.apps() do
      [%{name: name} | _others] -> crashed.(name, Tour.Docker.crash(name))
      [] -> Tour.UI.note(:error, "No app container is running.")
    end
  end)
end)

Kino.listen(scale_to, fn %{data: %{n: n}} ->
  Tour.UI.run_in(happened, "make", ["scale", "N=#{n}"])
end)

Tour.UI.stack([Kino.Layout.grid([kill, scale_to], columns: 2), happened])
```

